1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,474
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 19.

2
00:00:05,094 --> 00:00:07,518
Part f prints the dot product of A and B.

3
00:00:07,518 --> 00:00:13,223
For A equals one, two, three, and B equals four, minus five, six, what is printed?

4
00:00:14,923 --> 00:00:17,867
dot starts at zero, the identity for addition.

5
00:00:18,487 --> 00:00:22,249
i equals zero: one times four is four, so dot is four.

6
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:28,085
i equals one: two times minus five is minus ten, so dot is minus six.

7
00:00:28,705 --> 00:00:33,738
i equals two: three times six is eighteen, so dot is twelve, and that is printed.

8
00:00:35,337 --> 00:00:39,819
The dot product multiplies matching elements and adds the products.

9
00:00:39,819 --> 00:00:43,453
The single loop uses the same index i on both arrays.

10
00:00:45,054 --> 00:00:46,650
So the program prints twelve.

11
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:51,076
Losing the minus sign on minus five, which gives thirty two.

12
00:00:51,796 --> 00:00:56,235
Exam tip: write each product in the table with its sign before adding.

13
00:00:56,235 --> 00:00:59,633
Most wrong answers here come from a dropped minus sign.
